{
  "id": 8065369866315,
  "title": "Better Than Palette",
  "handle": "better-than-palette",
  "description": "<p>Most 10-shade palettes look generous until you layer them — similar depths blur together and turn muddy by noon. Better Than Palette runs on rom&amp;nd’s five-level lightness system: ten shades spaced across five systematic levels of light, so every layer builds deeper instead of blending into mush. Pick your garden and stack color like it’s math, not luck.</p>\n<h3>Key Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>5 levels of light</strong> — ten shades spaced across five systematic brightness levels, so layers deepen cleanly without muddiness</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Fingertip-first matte</strong> — the ultra-fine formula inherited from Better Than Eyes melts in with body heat and fixes with zero fallout</li>\n<li>\n<strong>4 glitter types</strong> — vaseline, aurora, shimmer, and glitter bomb mix distinct particle sizes for multi-dimensional sparkle</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Endlessly buildable</strong> — one palette covers bare daily looks through full-depth evening definition</li>\n<li>\n<strong>No tools required</strong> — every shade is designed to blend and fix with fingertips alone</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Shades</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>00 Light &amp; Glitter Garden</strong> — Ten pure glitters, zero mattes. Clear opal, champagne, rose gold, and iced lilac to layer over any look or wear alone.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>01 Pampas Garden</strong> — Peach, coral, and champagne gold over warm ivory. Bright shades that bloom like late spring.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>02 Mahogany Garden</strong> — Caramel, cinnamon, and molten gold deepening into chocolate for a golden hour glow.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>03 Rosebud Garden</strong> — Dusty rose, mauve, and soft pink beige. Cool toned calm with a quietly romantic finish.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>05 Shade &amp; Shadow Garden</strong> — An all-matte lineup of greige, sand, and cocoa in five even steps. The neutral backbone that shades and defines.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>07 Berry Fuchsia Garden</strong> — Fuchsia, p lum, and iced lavender against cool pinks. The boldest garden, made for evening.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>How to Use</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Base</strong> — Sweep the lightest matte across the lid as your foundation shade.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Build</strong> — Layer the next shades one by one, following the lightness order from light to deep.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Define</strong> — Press the deepest shades into the crease and outer corner for dimension.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Sparkle</strong> — Tap glitters onto the center of the lid with a fingertip; press, don’t sweep.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Check your work</strong> — Flip your camera to black and white and watch all five levels of depth show up on your lids.</li>\n</ol>",
